Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:23:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Tell the agent to run the setup check on first use

When Blender or Unreal does not answer, the agent runs the Game Harness setup
check and offers the fix, pointing at the Set up my machine recipe.
---
 ..._agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap | 2 ++
 .../snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__basic.snap  | 2 ++
 .../goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__one_extension.snap    | 2 ++
 .../goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__typical_setup.snap    | 2 ++
 crates/goose/src/prompts/system.md                              | 2 ++
 5 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap b/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap
index e7bf7d0..7822e38 100644
--- a/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap
+++ b/crates/goose/src/agents/snapshots/goose__agents__prompt_manager__tests__all_platform_extensions.snap
@@ -18,6 +18,8 @@ enough to try in Play in Editor, say exactly what to try, and wait for their ver
 - For a request with several parts (a mesh, textures, a sound, a Blueprint), plan it with the Game Harness and give independent parts
   to subagents in parallel, each with only the tools of its domain.
 - Never submit, push or check in on the developer's behalf; they decide what goes into version control.
+- On first use, or when Blender or Unreal does not answer, run the Game Harness setup check, explain what is missing,
+  and fix it only with the developer's agreement. The "Set up my machine" recipe walks through it.
 
